<p>Convert ASCII uppercase letters within the specified codepoint range. Null index means zero; null length means through the end.</p>
</section>

<section class="cxx entity method">
<h1 id="Arcadia_StringBuilder_removeCodePointsAt">Arcadia_StringBuilder_removeCodePointsAt</h1>
<pre><code>void
Arcadia_StringBuilder_removeCodePointsAt
  (
    Arcadia_Thread* thread,
    Arcadia_StringBuilder* self,
    Arcadia_SizeValue codePointIndex,
    Arcadia_SizeValue numberOfCodePoints
  );</code></pre>
<p>Remove a half-open codepoint range. A zero count at the end is valid.</p>
</section>

<section class="cxx entity method">
<h1 id="Arcadia_StringBuilder_replaceCodePointsAt">Arcadia_StringBuilder_replaceCodePointsAt</h1>
<pre><code>void
Arcadia_StringBuilder_replaceCodePointsAt
  (
    Arcadia_Thread* thread,
    Arcadia_StringBuilder* self,
    Arcadia_SizeValue codePointIndex,
    Arcadia_SizeValue numberOfCodePoints,
    Arcadia_Value value
  );</code></pre>
<p>Atomically replace a half-open codepoint range with a value accepted by insertAt. Self-replacement uses the original contents. An empty replacement deletes the range.</p>
</section>

